<title>UK: Britain's AEA buys Canada's ASC.</title>
<headline>Britain's AEA buys Canada's ASC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British science and engineering services business AEA Technology Plc said on Tuesday it had agreed to buy Canadian software company Advanced Scientific Computing Ltd (ASC Ltd) for C$15 million.</p>
<p>AEA said ASC, based in Ontario, had a net asset value of C$2.0 million at the end of March last year and annual turnover totalled C$5.0 million. It said the acquisition would be funded from internal resources.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
